1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20281, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Q3MjpjQXSygwWyP977pXpZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20281, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XZhetTPRbrctFNmZfseVV2", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20581, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XZhetTPRbrctFNmZfseVV2", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20581, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XZhetTPRbrctFNmZfseVV2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25829, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XcFrdQKWzSB4M5yXZhutSC", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so for a while the regions were running different versions. A second attempt finished the rollback. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56429, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XcFrdQKWzSB4M5yXZhutSC", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56429, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XcFrdQKWzSB4M5yXZhutSC", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58080, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DooShAFeX3QEWA8pducY5S", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58380, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DooShAFeX3QEWA8pducY5S", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58380, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DooShAFeX3QEWA8pducY5S", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62999, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Before the rollback, v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Retry:** The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east. That left the regions on different versions until I ran the same rollback again, which finished it.\n- **Current state:** All three regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so there's only one incident and on-call was paged once. It records what happened and two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CG612Dyaes7q3oR6Fy4j1k", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UaKUZjeq9StWKUPeaM81Me", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BE6emcNJcocRSmzjgAaQXW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SMk5H77TMNYqNgTS8npmvg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east rolled back. Rolling back to the same version again should be safe to repeat, so I'll retry once to finish the other regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Bfpv9rzdzapoLAxPyfqS3F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Q3MjpjQXSygwWyP977pXpZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XZhetTPRbrctFNmZfseVV2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XcFrdQKWzSB4M5yXZhutSC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so for a while the regions were running different versions. A second attempt finished the rollback. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01DooShAFeX3QEWA8pducY5S", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Before the rollback, v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Retry:** The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east. That left the regions on different versions until I ran the same rollback again, which finished it.\n- **Current state:** All three regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so there's only one incident and on-call was paged once. It records what happened and two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}